<p>President Donald Trump warned Iran on Sunday to act quickly, writing on Truth Social that “the Clock is Ticking” and that “there won’t be anything left of them” if Tehran did not move fast. The warning followed reports that Washington and Israel were discussing possible renewed military operations against Iran and that Trump had spoken with Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. The dispute centers on efforts to reach an agreement over Iran’s nuclear program and end the current conflict. Iran’s Mehr news agency said Washington offered “no concrete concessions” in response to Iranian proposals, while also seeking strict, long-term restrictions on Iran’s nuclear sector and negotiations as a condition for ending hostilities on all fronts. Several reports said Tehran was preparing a “mechanism” or fees for Strait of Hormuz traffic as fighting and diplomatic contacts continued.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/M4LOVTBvs4KGFsJq7-dgvOh7Vs9KmrNy2nt5tRqwEXeY6Z4FQZ7os2MpM-FJZjcySPSQJ9dWhIWCwFJnWJVFEW4LLWaJNNBEGDTP-IozCw' alt='US President Donald Trump' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Earlier signal: Before Sunday’s warning, Trump posted a military-themed image with the phrase “It Was The Calm Before The Storm,” which several reports linked to possible renewed action against Iran.</li><li>Iranian state TV: SIC Notícias reported that Iranian state television showed the Revolutionary Guard teaching the public how to handle weapons.</li><li>Lebanon strikes: Israel launched airstrikes in southern Lebanon despite an extension of a truce between Israel and Lebanon, NDTV and The Hindu reported in live updates.</li><li>Military options: Die Presse reported that scenarios under discussion ranged from limited strikes to ground operations.</li></ul><blockquote>For Iran, the Clock is Ticking, and they better get moving, FAST, or there won’t be anything left of them. TIME IS OF THE ESSENCE! - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian Foreign 